    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n`AssignCustomerCode` (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`) previously set the code to `<REGION>-<HASH8>` unconditionally. It now de-duplicates against existing owners:\n\n- Injects `OwnerRepository` (by type, per the OfficeFloor convention already used by `EnsureUniqueIdentity` / `AssignNamesakeCount`).\n- Computes the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code as before.\n- Collects the `customerCode`s of all existing owners. The owner being created isn't saved yet at this step, so it's correctly excluded from the collision set.\n- If the base code is unused, it's returned unchanged. Otherwise it appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and increments until it finds a value not already in use \u2014 the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes the code unique.\n\nThis runs before `AssignMembershipNumber`, so the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and every other value derived from the code pick up the de-duplicated value automatically.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) asserts the rule's guarantee \u2014 distinct owners always get distinct customerCodes \u2014 and passes.",
